# Vendored independent-review evidence. Byte-exact, not text.
#
# Every packet ships a SHA256.json that pins the exact content of the
# artifacts beside it, and reviewers verify against it. Git's default
# `text=auto` normalises CRLF to LF on commit, which silently rewrites those
# bytes: the working tree still hashes correctly, the committed blob does
# not, and the manifest stops verifying for anyone who checks it out. That
# happened — three artifacts (round4/results.json, round4b/results.json,
# round4b/c5-ci-evidence.json) were committed LF-normalised and no longer
# matched their own manifests until they were restored from the packets.
#
# `-text` disables all EOL conversion for this tree so what is committed is
# what the reviewer hashed. Do not "fix line endings" in here: the mixed
# endings ARE the artifact.
* -text
